Feature: Qualified structured request forms
  Scenario: Structured form corrections preserve complete native requests
    Then thirteen structured form corrections retain fields schemas identities and reversible preimages

  Scenario: Structured form drift cannot be applied partially
    Then changed structured form contracts fail before any request is rewritten

  Scenario: GitLab indexed hashes retain nested files and array identity
    Then Rack form parts preserve indexed objects nested binary bytes and field boundaries

  Scenario: GitLab JSON mode preserves null and empty collections
    Then GitLab forms select JSON without files and retain nullable and empty values

  Scenario: All thirteen native structured forms retain their qualified wire formats
    Then thirteen native structured operations send validated bodies and private credentials

  Scenario: Invalid structured fields fail before private transport
    Then malformed structured fields and files cannot reach a private HTTP endpoint

  Scenario: Bulk import source credentials stay private
    Then a private source token can populate a GitLab bulk import JSON field without appearing in output

  Scenario: Structured form choices are part of private approval
    Then changed GitLab form profiles and nested file paths invalidate private authority

  Scenario: GitLab form profile and fallback schemas remain explicit
    Then GitLab form selection validates its profile and preserves field schema fallbacks
